00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.160
Film Courage: Naomi, can you&nbsp;
explain what a story goal is?

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:05.520
Naomi Beaty, Writer, Screenwriting Teacher and&nbsp;
Consultant: Sure, the way I use it is really just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:12.560
that it's that ultimate goal that your whole story&nbsp;
is structured around. It's the thing that your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:17.920
protagonist is trying to achieve in the story.&nbsp;
Story goal is just the easiest way to describe it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:23.600
In Silence of the Lambs it's Clarice trying&nbsp;
to catch the serial killer Buffalo Bill,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:29.840
that's her story goal. It's the plot thing&nbsp;
that gives your entire story its structure.

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:33.040
Film Courage: Is the story&nbsp;
goal also the story engine?

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:39.280
Naomi: The character's pursuit of that story goal&nbsp;
I think is what creates the engine and the story.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:44.880
The protagonist trying to achieve that thing,&nbsp;
that's what drives the story forward. It's what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:50.000
moves the plot so yeah I think the story&nbsp;
goal is a necessary part of that engine.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:53.200
Film Courage: Can you give&nbsp;
us examples of story goals&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:56.480
that work? Effective ones and&nbsp;
then ones that don't work well?

00:00:56.480 --> 00:01:03.200
Naomi: Sure, so effective story goals will have&nbsp;
some external component right so they can be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:10.160
dramatized on screen in some way ineffective story&nbsp;
goals are are usually very internal and things&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:15.920
that we can't see a character taking action toward&nbsp;
we can't see them pursuing if you're writing a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:21.680
movie it's it's going to be easier to to write it&nbsp;
to structure it if there's some external action or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:28.640
at least a way for you to show us what the&nbsp;
character is doing and for us to understand what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:36.880
they're doing let's see another thing that makes&nbsp;
a story goal effective is if it's difficult enough&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:42.320
to achieve that it will take the whole movie to&nbsp;
achieve right you don't want something so easy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:50.320
or so quick that it would be achieved in one&nbsp;
scene or a couple of scenes because you need&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:58.160
it to be difficult enough that your character can&nbsp;
try to can attempt to achieve it over 100 minutes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:05.200
or whatever and that difficulty can come from the&nbsp;
goal itself can be difficult or it can also come&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:09.280
from there's just so much conflict in the way&nbsp;
right that your your character has a hard time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:14.560
achieving it because there's something or someone&nbsp;
trying to stop them if that does that make sense&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:21.440
it does so an internal goal is hard because we&nbsp;
unless it's a novel we can't really tell what's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:27.120
going on with the character yeah and I think that&nbsp;
yeah so in a something that's very internal would&nbsp;&nbsp;

